00:50:42,480 --> 00:50:44,040
it's going to be worth pre-answering

247
00:50:44,040 --> 00:50:45,200
some common objections.

248
00:50:47,920 --> 00:50:53,720
So one objection says, look, all theories are false.

249
00:50:53,720 --> 00:50:55,560
So don't go and tell me my theory's false.

250
00:50:55,560 --> 00:51:00,280
What matters is prediction.

251
00:51:00,280 --> 00:51:03,000
Now, this, by the way, is one of the stranger pieces

252
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:05,280
of philosophy that economists have picked up from readings

253
00:51:05,280 --> 00:51:06,360
philosophy of science.

254
00:51:06,360 --> 00:51:08,080
All theories are false.

255
00:51:08,080 --> 00:51:11,320
So how many decimal places?

256
00:51:11,320 --> 00:51:15,400
Are some theories true to one decimal place?

257
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:17,560
And again, when you think about more,

