01:57:43,160 --> 01:57:45,120
but Tullock also went out of his way

492
01:57:45,120 --> 01:57:46,320
to insult people in Sweden,

493
01:57:46,320 --> 01:57:48,920
and Buchanan went out of his way to be on his best behavior

494
01:57:48,920 --> 01:57:51,120
whenever he was within 1,000 miles of Sweden,

495
01:57:51,120 --> 01:57:56,120
but still, at least this is,

496
01:57:56,480 --> 01:57:59,280
there's something to this where top people wanna go

497
01:57:59,280 --> 01:58:02,680
and create, and have intellectual children,

498
01:58:02,680 --> 01:58:04,680
so they can have intellectual grandchildren,

499
01:58:04,680 --> 01:58:05,920
and intellectual great-grandchildren,

500
01:58:05,920 --> 01:58:07,640
because remember, the generational time in academia

501
01:58:07,640 --> 01:58:09,740
is only like five to 10 years.

502
01:58:09,740 --> 01:58:12,120
So you can have, you can really be, if you're 80,

503
01:58:12,120 --> 01:58:13,600
you could have great, great, great, great,

504
01:58:13,600 --> 01:58:15,320
great intellectual grandchildren

505
01:58:15,320 --> 01:58:17,860
churning, getting their PhDs and citing you,

506
01:58:17,860 --> 01:58:19,520
and how do you think those people

507
01:58:19,520 --> 01:58:22,280
have articles with 10,000 citations did it?

